    "depends_on": [
        {
            "name": "entity_id",
            "mustBeNonEmpty": true,
            "documentation": "The entity this statement is about: the finest entity the value directly describes (T17). Usually a subject; any entity may be described (a strain, a session), but a statement about a non-subject entity only says what that entity's class has no field for (T1, T17). (`entity_id`, and subjects only, until 2026-10-08.)",
            "must_refer_to_document_class": "entity"
        },
        {
            "name": "value_id",
            "mustBeNonEmpty": false,
            "documentation": "The standalone value document that holds this statement's value, shared by every statement that points at it (item 30). When present, this statement's own value and value descriptors are empty: the shared document states them. Batch check `standalone_value` (report-only first; #73 audit 2 D13): when this names a value document, that document is a STANDALONE value -- not a statement, relation or clock_alignment leaf, all of which are also values.",
            "must_refer_to_document_class": "value"
        },
        {
            "name": "coordinate_system_id",
            "mustBeNonEmpty": false,
            "documentation": "Optional: the coordinate system this statement's coordinates are in, one id. Decided by Jess Haley, 2026-10-27 [site frame is a coordinate system] (V_eta_go_forward_class_audit.md): a probe's site X/Y/Z-Coordinate values each link to the probe's one `coordinate_system`. Declared on `statement` so every direction inherits it. A value kind that cannot be read without one (the `position` mixin) declares it required, so a statement with that mixin must give it; did2.build and the cache's required-edge check read the chain's declarations together.",
            "must_refer_to_document_class": "coordinate_system"
        }
    ],
